6189 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 4049 0 R
/T (This temple design reflects traditional Kerala architectural heritage, featuring a distinctive multi-tiered sloping roof finished with clay tiles and decorative gables. The structure is characterized by its horizontal emphasis and timber- inspired detailing, which harmonize with the natural environment. The square floor plan and courtyard-centric layout are meticulously designed to facilitate ritualistic circumambulation, balancing ancient Vastu principles with a sense of peace and timelessness.)
/E (This temple design reflects traditional Kerala architectural heritage, featuring a distinctive multi-tiered sloping roof finished with clay tiles and decorative gables. The structure is characterized by its horizontal emphasis and timber- inspired detailing, which harmonize with the natural environment. The square floor plan and courtyard-centric layout are meticulously designed to facilitate ritualistic circumambulation, balancing ancient Vastu principles with a sense of peace and timelessness.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [57]
>>
endobj
